<%# Pets (D-pets-section): a section of their own, without becoming a silo.
    The tool cards below this carry most of the page; the prose only has to
    say why the vet visit is still on the Health page too. %>

<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    A pet is a dependent with a medical history, a monthly cost, a
    prescription, and no way to tell you what hurts. Most households keep
    all of that in their head, on a vet's reminder postcard, and in a photo
    roll nobody can search.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Pets page gives every animal a card and a page of their own: the
    care that's booked or due, the food and when it runs out, their papers
    and their pictures. Nothing is filed away from where it also belongs —
    a vet visit is still on the Health page, and the kibble is still a line
    in the budget.
  </p>
</section>
